  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 136 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe forecast beyond Sunday remains rather benign with low precip \nchances. The upper high remains west of the region and centered near \nthe Four Corners while stretching from California eastward to \nColorado. This will keep upper flow weak and mostly out of the north \nover the FA, a not-so-favorable but also not-impossible pattern for \nstorms. Highly isolated diurnal storms could be possible if any \nweaknesses rotate around the upper high or if any of the weak \nsurface fronts progged to our north mid to late week can push into \nthe FA. Though afternoons will still be hot, they should not be as \nhot as last week due to the upper high being further westward. Highs \nwill average in the upper 90s on the Caprock and around/just over \n100 off the Caprock.",
